 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Holding a shard to Senya's neck, the inspector forces the chefs back, makes them punch Fedya for seducing his wife, and flees up the stairs toward the roof while Denis stumbles in and unties Kostya and Nastya.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Всем назад, не подходите ко мне!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, делайте всё, что просит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "А теперь быстро подтяни штаны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Не буду я это делать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Я тебе сказал, подтяни штаны!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "А ты давай, ударь его.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Не подходите ко мне сейчас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мы ещё можем спокойно договориться!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Нет, вам всем теперь конец!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Сеня, беги за ним наверх!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Денис, спасибо, ты мой спаситель!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Можешь жить у меня бесплатно!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Всем назад, не подходите ко мне!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone back, do not come near me!' The grammar packs 'to everyone' and 'to me' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, делайте всё, что просит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Please do everything that he asks.' The meaning hinges on 'please' working together with 'is asking for' in spoken Russian. the inspector answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "А теперь быстро подтяни штаны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And now pull up your pants quickly.' In Russian, the idea of 'and' flows naturally into 'pants' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Не буду я это делать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am not going to do that.' In Russian, the idea of 'not' flows naturally into 'to do' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Я тебе сказал, подтяни штаны!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I told you, pull up your pants!' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'pants' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "А ты давай, ударь его.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And you go on, hit him.' the inspector anchors the line on 'and', while 'his' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Не подходите ко мне сейчас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not come near me right now!' The grammar packs 'not' and 'now' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мы ещё можем спокойно договориться!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We can still reach an agreement calmly!' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'we', while 'to reach an agreement' completes the thought. the inspector answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Нет, вам всем теперь конец!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, this is the end for all of you now!' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'no' before landing on 'end'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Сеня, беги за ним наверх!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, run upstairs after him!' The meaning hinges on 'Senya' working together with 'upstairs' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Денис, спасибо, ты мой спаситель!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Denis, thank you, you are my savior!' Senya addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'savior'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Можешь жить у меня бесплатно!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
